v1.20 - a port without a serial-starter node is not automatically foreign
  driver: v1.19 skipped a candidate port whenever serial-starter had no node
  for it. That is one inference too many: this driver removes the node itself
  when it claims a port, and the node does not come back until the next
  reboot. After a restart of the process the driver would find its own port
  without a node and refuse it. The MaxxFan driver, which had the same rule,
  lost its card from a customer system for exactly this reason.
  A port without a node is now only left alone when another process really
  holds it open, read from /proc rather than inferred. Ports that
  serial-starter never managed are covered by the same change.

